<section id="price-spread-analysis">
  <h2>3. Price Spread &amp; Market Competitiveness</h2>
  <p>
    Price spread is the most policy-relevant dimension for assessing market competitiveness. 
    A narrow interquartile range (IQR) suggests most consumers face similar prices; a wide IQR or large 
    max-min range indicates meaningful disparities that may warrant regulatory attention.
